            {
              "type": "History and physical note",
              "title": "New Patient Preventive Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2022-09-14T09:35",
              "body": "Wendy is a 25-year-old woman establishing care. Wants a physical and a doctor she can text. Works in business development for a software firm, a lot of calls and some travel. Feels well. No complaints today.\n\nPMH: none. No hospitalizations.\nPSH: wisdom teeth out at 18.\nMeds: none. No supplements.\nAllergies: none to medications.\nFH: mother has bipolar I disorder. Paternal grandfather had major depression. No known heart disease, diabetes or cancer in parents.\nSocial: single, lives in town. Has never smoked. Does not drink at all. No drug use. Walks and does a spin class twice a week.\nGyn: regular cycles. Last Pap 2021 at her old office, normal per pt; records requested.\nImmunizations: HPV series as a teen, Tdap 2019 per her old office.\n\nROS: negative across systems. Sleep 7 hrs. Mood good. PHQ-2 0.\n\nExam: well appearing, pleasant, organized. Vitals in flowsheet. HEENT unremarkable, TMs clear. Thyroid not enlarged. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear bilaterally. Abdomen soft, nontender. Skin without rashes or concerning lesions. Neuro grossly intact. Calm, euthymic, linear thought.\n\nAssessment and plan:\n1. Health maintenance, 25F. Baseline CBC, CMP, lipids and TSH drawn. One-time HIV and hep C screens drawn, she agrees. Flu vaccine today, right deltoid. Pap not due until 2024.\n2. Family history of bipolar disorder in her mother: noted. She has no history of mood episodes herself.\nReturn in a year for a physical, sooner as needed."
            }
